+### M161 — Later access to the notification-claim cable is reported; reliance remains inferred
+
+**Original ID:** CC001. **Type:** Review-reported access plus explicitly conditional inference.
+
+CIA OIG printed67 / physical92 reports July2,2001 access to SCALEC134684 dated January5,2000, before the July13 revisit recommendation, and a July23 follow-up. The cable asserted that travel documents had reached the FBI.
+
+- The review explicitly says the reason for the early access is unclear and treats the reader’s likely belief that the FBI already knew as an inference. No native audit, cable, recipient receipt or contemporaneous reader explanation was acquired.
+- The January5,2001 identification-cable quotation elsewhere on the same page and January5,2000 SCALEC134684 reference are different source descriptions; neither is silently changed.
+- M154 already records the unconfirmed notification assertion. This entry adds the later-access/reliance question, not a second independent proof of delivery failure or deliberate misinformation.
