+### M164 — Official notification accounts differ in flight identity as well as stated times
+
+**Original ID:** FA001. **Type:** Conflicting published official accounts.
+
+The reproduced September18,2001 NORAD release and FAA table give AA77 notification09:24 and UA93N/A or NA. May23,2003 testimony gives UA93 possible-hijack notice09:16. The 2004 Commission account gives first NEADS UA93 notice10:07, AA77 missing09:34, and identifies the09:24 log entry as phantom AA11.
+
+- Preserve all versions. The shift09:16 to10:07 is51 minutes of stated anchors, not a calibrated operational delay or measured clock offset. A missing-aircraft notice, hijack notice and inferred flight identity are different events.
+- The 2001 NORAD release also gives UA17508:43 and estimated crashes09:37/10:03 for AA77/UA93; the FAA table gives UA17509:05 and09:38/10:04 crashes. These facsimile values are retained without normalization.
+- No independent reconstruction of native radar, phone recordings, log entries or clocks was performed. The Commission’s correction claim is itself preserved as a source position, not selected as controlling by this audit.
+
+**Exact locations:** [source review](../../broader-evidence/outstanding-records-verification-2026-10-26/REPORT.md#fa001); report SHA-256`45305b69c35bba07365b60e0ea130d0a33a066ac059f6cdcb38841b0036106a0`. Register locators retain source hashes, pages/paragraphs and derivative excerpt-line ranges. For FA012, AUDIO-CONTROL-CHECK.json and METHOD-PINS.json identify local method assets.
